@title Route 9 Corridor: Decision for Council
@subtitle Riverbend City Council vote on 2026-12-02
@author Transportation Department
@date 2026-12-02

!!! The department needs the council's approval on 2026-12-02 to meet the federal grant deadline. The application is due 2027-01-31 and requires a council-approved option.

## Options

grid 3

### Enhanced bus
More frequent buses and signal priority at lights.
- Capital cost: $85M
- Build time: 2 years
- Riders by 2035: 14000 per weekday
- Operating cost: $22M a year

### Bus rapid transit
Dedicated lanes and stations. **Recommended.**
- Capital cost: $310M
- Build time: 4 years
- Riders by 2035: 26000 per weekday
- Operating cost: $31M a year

### Light rail
Rail service on the corridor.
- Capital cost: $940M
- Build time: 8 years
- Riders by 2035: 38000 per weekday
- Operating cost: $44M a year

## Capital cost per rider

data cpr = option,dollars per weekday rider; Enhanced bus,6100; Bus rapid transit,11900; Light rail,24700

chart hbar cpr unit=$ labels focus="Bus rapid transit" title="Capital cost per weekday rider"

A federal grant can cover up to 50% of capital cost.

## Trade-offs

- **Enhanced bus** is cheap and fast to deliver, but carries the fewest riders and still shares congested lanes.
- **Bus rapid transit** is the middle path and could be upgraded to rail later.
- **Light rail** carries the most riders and attracts development, but takes 8 years and the city could not fund its share without a bond measure.

## Recommendation

The department recommends **bus rapid transit**.

! Council approval is needed on 2026-12-02 to meet the 2027-01-31 federal grant application deadline.
